              "type": "text",
              "text": "What is least number of distinct points needed to uniquely determine a logarithmic curve that passes through all of the points?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "3 suitable distinct points.",
      "worked": "The family studied, $y=k\\log_a(bx+c)+d$, has three independent parameters: a horizontal shift determining the vertical asymptote, a vertical scale and a vertical shift. Three suitable points can determine these parameters. This assumes that the points are compatible with a nonconstant logarithmic curve and determine it uniquely.",
